### **ii. Climatic suitability**

#### **Entire period: 1981--2025**

Over the entire 44-year period (1981–2025), predicted cold stress for EAB decreased significantly across portions of the northern United States, particularly the Upper Midwest, although localized increases occurred in parts of Montana (@fig-eab-cold-stress). During the same period, predicted heat stress increased significantly across parts of the South and West (@fig-eab-heat-stress). When annual accumulated stress units exceed limits specified in DDRP models, climatic suitability may change. Significant shifts in climatic suitability for EAB were relatively limited, indicating that accumulated stress generally remained within the limits defining suitability. Increases in suitability were concentrated in portions of the Southwest (@fig-eab-suitability).


