:::
:::


#### **Recent period: 2001--2025**

Trends in climate stress for EAB over the recent 24-year period (2001–2025) differed in several respects. Predicted cold stress increased across portions of the Upper Midwest, with few areas showing significant decreases (@fig-eab-cold-stress-recent), contrasting with the widespread decreases observed over the longer period. Heat stress continued to increase across the Southwest and Lower Midwest but decreased in parts of the interior West, southern California, and Arizona (@fig-eab-heat-stress-recent). As during the longer period, changes in climatic suitability remained spatially localized, suggesting that recent shifts in cold and heat stress translated into relatively limited changes in predicted establishment suitability (@fig-eab-suitability-recent).


